We propose UP-VLA, which unifies MMU and future prediction in one autoregressive backbone. Our contributions are:
(1) UP-VLA, a unified VLA jointly trained on MMU and future prediction;
(2) a unified prompting and attention-masking strategy that mixes continuous MMU tokens and discrete predictive tokens in a single LLM;
(3) a joint prediction-and-understanding action mechanism conditioning actions on semantic scene descriptions and predicted futures;
(4) state-of-the-art results on CALVIN (ABC$\rightarrow$D average length 4.08, +33\% over GR-1) and real-world gains in semantic generalization and precision.

