In \cref{fig:real} (20 trials per task), LLM-backbone methods outperform RT-1 and Diffusion Policy on seen tasks, with UP-VLA competitive or best. On unseen-object grasping UP-VLA-RT-2 beats UP-VLA-phi-w/o-mmu, showing the semantic benefit of MMU, while UP-VLA is best overall. On precision tasks the order reverses (UP-VLA-phi-w/o-mmu above UP-VLA-RT-2), reflecting the benefit of future prediction for spatial detail, and UP-VLA is again best.

\subsection{Ablations}
