\Cref{table:ablate} ablates components. Removing prediction collapses ABC$\rightarrow$D performance from 4.08 to 1.44, so prediction is crucial for spatial and dynamics grounding. Removing Bridge pre-training drops it to 2.74, showing predictive pre-training matters. Removing MMU barely changes CALVIN (3.89) and seen real-world tasks (0.85) but lowers unseen-object success from 0.58 to 0.20, so MMU is critical for semantic generalization; removing only the MMU conditioning of actions also lowers it (0.50; CALVIN 3.99), so conditioning actions on scene descriptions helps. With 20-trial real-world evaluations, small differences (e.g. 0.80 vs. 0.85 seen) are within noise.

